A train travels at constant speed along a straight horizontal track towards an observer standing adjacent to the track, as shown in Fig. 6.1.

{{figure:figure_6_1.png}}

The train sounds its horn continuously as it approaches the observer. The horn emits a sound of constant frequency $251\,\mathrm{Hz}$. The frequency of sound heard by the observer is $291\,\mathrm{Hz}$. The speed of sound in air is $340\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$.
